// Bun Snapshot v1, https://bun.sh/docs/test/snapshots

exports[`golden snapshots of every human view root help: root-help 1`] = `
"--- stdout ---
Agent Profile Kit composes reusable agent material into host-native projects.

Usage: apkit <command> [arguments]

First run:
  apkit init
  apkit install <profile> --host <host>
  apkit status
  apkit update

  Choose a Profile with apkit guide profile; see apkit install --help for
    supported Host values.

Common commands:
  init
    Initialize or adopt the canonical Workspace and settings
  guide
    Show a topic index, full Workspace guidance, or one focused authoring
      example
  new
    Create a Skill, Context Module, or Profile scaffold in the configured
      Workspace
  open
    Open the configured Workspace in your system file manager
  install
    Install a Profile with Agent Hosts into a Project and remember the
      selection
  validate
    Check Workspace and settings validity
  configure
    Change a reusable Profile's Context and Skill membership without editing
      files
  status
    Show the complete read-only update plan for the complete fleet, the
      containing Project, or one explicit Project
  update
    Sync the complete fleet, the containing Project, or one explicit Project
  details
    Show retained lifecycle operation history: the latest run, a compact list,
      or one run by identity

More commands:
  Inventory:
  list
    List read-only inventory for Projects, Profiles, or Hosts
  Teardown:
  uninstall
    Remove selected Project installations and forget their recorded selection;
      a lone --profile reaches that Profile's installations fleet-wide; --host
      removes only those Hosts within the scope
  Machine details:
  info
    Show the engine version and selected application locations

For deeper Workspace authoring guidance (Context Modules, Skills, Profiles,
  and bindings), run apkit guide --full.
--- stderr ---
"
`;

